.TH DIFFVIM-JOGGER 1 "2026-08-16" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim-jogger \- exercise diffvim across many option combinations on synthetic test cases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim-jogger
.RI [ output_dir ]
.br
.B diffvim-jogger
.B \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim-jogger
generates 18 small synthetic test file pairs covering common
insertion/deletion patterns (mid-line replacement, insert at start,
delete at end, block delete, unicode, indent change, etc.), then runs
.B diffvim
in log mode 2 with each of ~25 option combinations on every test pair,
writing one log file per (combination, case) into the results directory.
A Markdown report is also written summarising the test cases and the
option combinations.

The tool is useful for visual inspection: open any two log files in the
same combo directory to compare how a single option changes the
animation for the same input.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I output_dir
Where to write test cases, logs, and the report (default:
.IR /tmp/diffvim-jogger ).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH OUTPUT STRUCTURE
.PP
.RS
.nf
<output_dir>/
\fBtest_cases/\fP    18 pairs of <name>_old.txt / <name>_new.txt
\fBresults/\fP
    combo_0_<combo_name>/
        01_mid_replace_same.log
        02_mid_replace_shorter.log
        ...
    combo_1_<combo_name>/
        ...
\fBREPORT.md\fP       summary of all test cases and option combos
.fi
.RE

.SH TEST CASES
The 18 test cases cover:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
Mid-line replacement (same / shorter / longer)
.IP \(bu 3
Insert at beginning / end / middle
.IP \(bu 3
Delete at beginning / end / middle
.IP \(bu 3
Insert + trailing delete (the delete-end-first case)
.IP \(bu 3
Multiple changes on the same line
.IP \(bu 3
Complete line replacement
.IP \(bu 3
Identical char run deletion (e.g. \-\-\-\-\-\-\-)
.IP \(bu 3
Multi-line block deletion / insertion
.IP \(bu 3
Unicode characters
.IP \(bu 3
Indent-only change
.IP \(bu 3
Mixed insert+delete across multiple positions
.RE

.SH OPTION COMBINATIONS
Around 25 combinations are exercised, including:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
Baseline (no flags)
.IP \(bu 3
Post-processing: --optimize-sequence, --left-to-right
.IP \(bu 3
Deletion speed: --rapid-eol-delete, --accel-delete, --word-accel,
--adaptive-word-delete, --rapid-identical-chars
.IP \(bu 3
Highlight: --highlight-inline, --highlight-hunk, --highlight-word,
--dim-unchanged
.IP \(bu 3
Overwrite + delete-end-first: --overwrite, --delete-end-first,
--delete-end-first-smart, and their combinations
.IP \(bu 3
Presets: --preset fast-delete, --preset review, --preset ai-code
.IP \(bu 3
Several combined combos
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_BIN
Override the
.B diffvim
binary to invoke (default:
.IR <script_dir>/diffvim ).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B diffvim-jogger
Run with default output directory.
.TP
.B diffvim-jogger /tmp/myjog
Use a custom output directory.
.TP
.B diffvim-jogger && open /tmp/diffvim-jogger/REPORT.md
Run and immediately open the report.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR diffvim-compare (1)
.br
.I docs/OPTION_COMBINATIONS.md
and
.I docs/POST_PROCESSING.md
describe the option semantics in detail.

> **Note:** The project now uses an external pipeline (diffvim-compute-cpp → diffvim-postprocess → diffvim-pace → animator). See `docs/PIPELINE.md` and `docs/DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` for the current architecture. Coloring (`diffvim-colorize`), streaming mode (`--stream`), and typed delays are described in the Developer Guide.
